19th January 1985 WIMBLEDON 10M Championship

In what was one of the lowest, if not the lowest, turn outs in 25 years Carl Lawton regained the championship. Didn't he first win in 1972? Neil Foster produced an excellent performance for 2nd and a personal best, and John Newnham's experience got him 3rd.

