14th APRIL 1985 WIMBLEDON SOUTHERN 12 STAGE RELAY

Last minute efforts by Clive Shippen helped prevent the Southern 12 Stage Relay being switched by the SCAAA's to the unpopular Thamesmead site. With a rejuvinated Belgrave Hall we were able to provide a worthy base for this year's race and it is to be hoped that we will be honoured with this event in the years ahead.

Sadly our team couldn't match the hopes of our supporters and as in most recent years our top men reported unfit for duty although some of them jogging around the course seemed pretty fit to the casual observers. Andy North proved fastest of the short leg runners with the amazing 53 year old Laurie O'Hara second best. On the long leg Oliver showed little sign of his previous days 10km p.b. while Mike Hayes again ran exceptionally well.

